{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1502233-storypath-chase-scenes","id":1502233,"title":"[Storypath] Chase Scenes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion","Storypath System"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-05T13:29:35-08:00","id":1502233,"title":"[Storypath] Chase Scenes","content":"How to run enemies chasing PCs across few thousands kilometres? \ud83e\udd14 Is it Complex and Opposed action, this chase? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-06-2023, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T00:12:58-08:00","id":1502289,"title":"","content":"In my example - Chase would be from Singapore to Bangalore - it's average 7000km ( circa 120 h ) by car or 4 hours by plane. ( Modern tech of 2020s )<br /> <br /> IF going by Complex Action rules - What Milestones like for 7000 km by car - and what like 4 hours by plane? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-06-2023, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T05:09:20-08:00","id":1502297,"title":"","content":"Depends on how much attention you want to give it.<br /> You want a kilometer per kilometer race? Do a lot of rolling, maybe every hour or pursuing, in the middle as the characters get closer or take distance of the chaser/pursuer.<br /> You want to make it just to define time difference between them? Maybe every 1000 km you roll to check how distant they are.<br /> Want just to check if they kept track of the other? Do a single roll and that\u2019s it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T05:28:22-08:00","id":1502299,"title":"","content":"Very ambiguous answer - I have to think about it...<br /> <br /> <img width=\"220\" height=\"220\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.tenor.com/4Nh-kwo0mSQAAAAM/batman-thinking.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/4Nh-kwo0mSQAAAAM/batman-thinking.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/4Nh-kwo0mSQAAAAM/batman-thinking.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T13:37:47-08:00","id":1502321,"title":"","content":"So, returning after some deliberations...<br /> <br /> I want this great 7000 km chase to be whole game session. Best would be some actions scenes on the roof of the speeding train - but we will see what players will come up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> None the less, if this will be whole game session - I think I need to refrain Milestones to collect a bit...<br /> <br /> 1. <b>As it is whole session Chase, I need to balance dice rolling - if any. \ud83e\udd14</b> Making it 4 Milestones only to get by 4 rolls will end fun clearly too fast. Making it 120 rolls by each hour - or even only by 24 rolls to get - will probably be too tedious. Now thinking about it... <b>Maybe make 12 Milestones, 1 per each 10 hours of car drive?</b> And then would be 8 or 12 Milestones per plane flight - each Milestone per 20 or 30 minutes of flight?<br /> <br /> 2. Can Milestone be changed for action scene? Like instead on nearest rolling, if Milestones numbers are close - enemies are getting just after your teams vehicle. Then view switch to enemies jumping from their car onto yours, trying to throw you off - or kill you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And then I assume this action scene is counted as next Milestone in whole Chase? Like in that scene....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_gxH7K95U7Q\" data-code=\"_gxH7K95U7Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_gxH7K95U7Q/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-12-2023, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T16:53:47-08:00","id":1502331,"title":"","content":"You can have any set of rolls for each milestone. For example, you may have a milestone focused in they taking a off road trip to avoid a road block that and up with they needing to spend the night in the woods (survival as skill) and another of them driving through a city avoiding the police (using Larceny) and another scene that is basically a road trip with some obstacles (requiring pilot).<br /> <br /> Personally, unless the story is focused in the trip itself, going by car will be extremely boring, as they will need to sleep, refil the tank, take some time to eat. So you can have the many different scenes of a trip movie or can just jump to the end, as it\u2019s not going to be THAT much of an action most time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T00:04:06-08:00","id":1502351,"title":"","content":"This is a cinematic game trying to emulate action movies.<br /> <br /> In an action movie like Mission Impossible would you see scenes of people travelling for hours on end from one continent to the next? No, that would be boring. You just skip right to the new place (with a nice overhead shot and a text saying where we are now) to get to the action.<br /> <br /> If I had the characters go for an international continent chase that takes days then chase rules are entirerly the wrong approach. Use the Milestone system instead with maybe 3-5 rolls. These are just some examples:<br /> 1) Technology + Wits to have the hacker trace their quarry through the technology they use.<br /> 2) Academics/Enigmas + Intellect to figure out the best route to take to avoid notice.<br /> 3) Persuasion + Manipulation to have the face character call in a few favors to slow their quarry down.<br /> 4) Integrity + Composure to make straight-faced lies when the corrupt police tries to slow the characters down.<br /> 5) Drive + Wits to stalk the quarry discretely.<br /> <br /> Any failures during these rolls will accumulate Complications such as:<br /> - The characters strain themselves to get there on time and are hungry and tired when they reach their quarry.<br /> - The characters draw too much attention to themselves and get on the news.<br /> - Some corrupt police are sent to deal with the characters.<br /> - The quarry becomes well aware that they are followed and organize an ambush or gather more allies.<br /> <br /> Once the characters get to their quarry THEN you can break out chase rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T08:06:39-08:00","id":1502391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1502233-storypath-chase-scenes?p=1502351#post1502351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had the characters go for an international continent chase that takes days then chase rules are entirerly the wrong approach. Use the Milestone system instead with maybe 3-5 rolls. These are just some examples:<br /> 1) Technology + Wits to have the hacker trace their quarry through the technology they use.<br /> 2) Academics/Enigmas + Intellect to figure out the best route to take to avoid notice.<br /> 3) Persuasion + Manipulation to have the face character call in a few favors to slow their quarry down.<br /> 4) Integrity + Composure to make straight-faced lies when the corrupt police tries to slow the characters down.<br /> 5) Drive + Wits to stalk the quarry discretely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great examples - But in my sample, players are chased down, not are chasing. So NPCs should roll those example rolls against players? Like players are hiding their trails in mountain ( Survival + Intellect, maybe? ) and antagonists are rolling to find them ( Survival + Cunning )? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T08:23:45-08:00","id":1502395,"title":"","content":"My suggestion is you give a certain number of \u201cfree successes\u201d to start with, representing the head start the characters have over the pursuers.<br /> <br /> Each milestone the characters spend their successes to do their regular actions and the extra successes they can spend to gain advantage (add to the pool), representing they did their chores under the expected time and so they hit the road faster. The pursuers do the same in their turn, except they subtract those successes from the pool (with the characters not knowing how well they are doing over the pursuers).<br /> <br /> If the poll reach 0, the pursuers reached the characters at some point, and the real action will start.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say they reach and there was a big fight in the road, with shots between vehicles. If the characters break all the pursuers vehicles they will be left behind and the characters gain a new pool of successes representing the pursuers fixing their vehicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T03:41:58-08:00","id":1502598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1502233-storypath-chase-scenes?p=1502391#post1502391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great examples - But in my sample, players are chased down, not are chasing. So NPCs should roll those example rolls against players? Like players are hiding their trails in mountain ( Survival + Intellect, maybe? ) and antagonists are rolling to find them ( Survival + Cunning )? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>If the players are the ones trying to get away you just do the exact same thing: they roll various rolls to try to outrun or outsmart their pursuers. I personally do not roll for NPCs, I just set a difficulty for them to beat, but you do you.<br /> <br /> The whole chase could be like a montage in a movie with every roll representing a key dramatic scene in that montage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T09:36:51-08:00","id":1502844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1502233-storypath-chase-scenes?p=1502395#post1502395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion is you give a certain number of \u201cfree successes\u201d to start with, representing the head start the characters have over the pursuers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What should be 'celling' to lose the pursuers? 20 success? 40 successes by players? 15+ successes OVER the persuers? How to balance rolls? What should be Difficulty for each Milestone - 3 Diff, 5 Diff, 7 Diff? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Better to set number of Milestones to 6 - or to 12 maybe? <br /> <br /> I think I simply would get characters 1 Milestone on 'head start' - and then the chase starts? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1502233-storypath-chase-scenes?p=1502395#post1502395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each milestone the characters spend their successes to do their regular actions and the extra successes they can spend to gain advantage (add to the pool), representing they did their chores under the expected time and so they hit the road faster. The pursuers do the same in their turn, except they subtract those successes from the pool (with the characters not knowing how well they are doing over the pursuers).<br /> <br /> If the poll reach 0, the pursuers reached the characters at some point, and the real action will start.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say they reach and there was a big fight in the road, with shots between vehicles. If the characters break all the pursuers vehicles they will be left behind and the characters gain a new pool of successes representing the pursuers fixing their vehicles.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"640\" height=\"320\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.tenor.com/u-PA4O5_KMkAAAAd/seriously.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/u-PA4O5_KMkAAAAd/seriously.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/u-PA4O5_KMkAAAAd/seriously.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T19:17:52-08:00","id":1502907,"title":"","content":"It depends on you as a SG want the, to be reached or not. I think you are over complicating a decision you could do without rolling dice.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I personally would do as I want, and the players would have to deal with it. The idea of adding scenes to the story on the fly can have some unwanted results. It\u2019s not like you are opening new ways, it\u2019s more kind of needing to plan for additional scenes that probably won\u2019t happen (or probably will).<br /> <br /> If your pursuers are as good as the characters, giving 6 successes will make them never reach them, if they are better, the result is the opposite, they will reach sooner or latter, and it\u2019s a LONG trip to think as a chase.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t even know it they will fly or drive. If they drive, and the pursuers know when\u2019re they are going, they would fly and reach the destination before (days before), and if they fly, there is not much open space to roll, as they will be in the plane, pretty high and out of reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T23:37:25-08:00","id":1503206,"title":"","content":"So... Thinking more about topic...<br /> <br /> I will probably make 6 Milestones for PCs to get to run away - with enemies traps or rolls as Difficulties for PCs rolls. They can even bypass Failure rolls by making quick scene where enemies are chasing they up - and PCs need to stop them. It can get up to Milestones 9, if things gone very bad for PCs.<br /> <br /> For example, <b>PCs roll poorly on roll for 3rd Milestone</b>, they get suddenly small car chase scene where enemies are right after them, in their mirrors. If they get to solve the problem to 'take out' enemies car ( like maybe throwing down the gasoline barrel and shooting on vehicle ), <b><u>Milestone is marked as checked</u></b>, in the end. If not - enemies will get them, as kind of 'double Failure' then.<br /> <br /> How does this interpretation sounds? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-16-2023, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T23:59:41-08:00","id":1503207,"title":"","content":"I like it. Sounds balanced in quantity and quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T12:13:21-08:00","id":1504477,"title":"","content":"So run today game session with two chases - one was street chase. Second was long chase, for five days. I used them both on 6 milestones each. From my observation, even on enemies 10 +3 Enh dicepool is quenched by 4 players rolling teamwork - enemies got 10 success, players get up to 25 in one attempt roll on Milestone. <img src=\"ht